          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points by matching the exposed ends of the domino line (The Caravan) and hitting the Flower number, while avoiding the Scorpion number.',
          gameplay: "1. Caravan Master: Rolls all four dice to set the Flower and Scorpion values for the round.\n2. The Lead: The Caravan Master plays any tile to start the line.\n3. Matching: Players must match one end of the 'Caravan'. If unable, they must draw from the 'Oasis'.\n4. Doubles: Played across the line, creating more matching combinations for scoring.",
          keyRules: [
            "The Scorpion's Sting: You can be forced to play a 'Scorpion' tile if no other legal moves exist, taking the penalty points.",
            "Domino: The first player to exhaust their hand ('dominoes') wins the round and receives a bonus (usually 2 chips).",
            'Winning condition: Score points by matching the exposed ends of the domino line (The Caravan) and hitting the Flower number, while avoiding the Scorpion number.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize matching the ends for Bergenndstyle points. The dice bonuses are great, but the points for double-matching (2 or 3 points) are the foundation of a win.',
          intermediate: 'Scorpion Sabotage: If you can track which player is short on tiles, try to lead a number that forces them to play a Scorpion tile, hitting them with penalty points just as they think they are about to domino.',
          advanced: "Freezing the Oasis: If you have a strong lead, try to play tiles that force opponents to draw heavily from the Oasis. Once it's empty, you can 'block' the game if you have the lowest remaining pips.",
          tips: [
            'Hold the Flower tile as long as possible. If you can end the round by playing it on a matching end, you maximize your score in a single turn.',
            'Blanks are your safest cardsâ€”they can never be the Flower or the Scorpion (since dice only have 1-6).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
